  << /ActualText (Anna M\374ller \05034\051 is a customer service specialist in Berlin who has built a stable career over the past eight years\054 but recently feels increasing anxiety as automation and AI tools begin to replace parts of her daily work\056 On a typical day\054 she handles repetitive support tickets through systems like Zendesk and CRM tools\054 while LinkedIn constantly reminds her that \034customer support roles are disappearing\056\035 During lunch breaks and evenings\054 she searches for career advice on Google\054 Reddit\054 YouTube\054 and platforms like Udemy or Coursera\054 but quickly becomes overwhelmed by too many career options and generic recommendations that don\031t match her background\056 She often bookmarks courses but hesitates to commit\054 fearing she will waste time and money on the wrong path\056 After work\054 mental fatigue and constant comparison to others on LinkedIn lowers her confidence further\056 Anna doesn\031t want endless options or motivational advice \024 she wants clear validation of her existing strengths\054 a focused skill gap analysis\054 and a structured learning roadmap that helps her upskill efficiently and feel confident that her effort will lead to real career progress\056)
